The Iran Conflict and Implications for Global Technology
</h3>


                <p class="mt-12 text-tertiary f-heading-3">April 29-29, 2026</p>

                <p class="mt-space-1 text-secondary f-caption-2">1-2 PM ET</p>

                <div class="mt-space-4 text-secondary f-body-2">
                    <p>The conflict involving the U.S. and Iran has added uncertainty into global energy markets, trade flows and technology supply chains across the Middle East. Rising energy costs, shipping disruptions and broader regional instability affect the consumer technology industry in areas such as logistics, input availability and market conditions. The conversation will focus on external market conditions, emerging risks and high-level scenario planning to help companies better understand the evolving landscape. </p>
                </div>

